  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1402.01 Applicability of Chapter",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1402.01 Applicability of Chapter.\n\n(a) This chapter shall apply to:\n\n(1) Used oil, as defined in Env-Hw 104, except as specified otherwise in this part;\n\n(2) Used oil generated, transported, collected, or marketed for purposes of recycling, including by being reused, re-refined, reclaimed, burned for energy recovery, or processed; and\n\n(3) Used oil burned for energy recovery.\n\n(b) Used oil that is destined to be recycled and also exhibits a hazardous waste characteristic, due to contamination through use and not as a result of being mixed with a hazardous waste, shall be subject to regulation under this chapter instead of Env-Hw 100 through Env-Hw 800 and Env-Hw 1200.\n\n(c) If used oil is disposed of or is not destined to be recycled, the used oil shall be regulated as NH01 listed hazardous waste pursuant to Env-Hw 402.06(c) and subject to regulation under Env-Hw 100 through Env-Hw 800 and Env-Hw 1200 instead of this chapter.\n\n(d) Used oil subject to RSA 339-B:2 and RSA 339-B:2-a shall be handled in accordance with the applicable requirements of this chapter.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
